**Finding submitted: MISSING (medium severity, transition)**

**What I found.** Section 4 of the Agreement ("Term; Termination; Termination Payment," p0023–p0029) deals only with notice periods and the calculation/payment of the Termination Payment. Nothing in the Agreement addresses what happens to our property or the Site on exit:

- HDI holds and operates the computer system storing the Site (p0009) and receives all of our Content (p0016);
- HDI is expressly exposed to our "Content, user information, data" as Confidential Information (p0048), but Section 8 imposes only non-use/non-disclosure duties — no return or destruction obligation;
- searches for "return" and "Content" produced no exit, export, migration or deletion language anywhere;
- Section 10.7 survival (p0068) lists only Sections 6.3, 7, 9 and 10 — so any new Section 4 obligation needs its own survival hook.

**Redline (validated ok:true).** Inserted a new Section 4.3 immediately after p0029, at the end of the termination section, requiring HDI on any expiry or termination to (a) provide up to six months of transition assistance at then-current rates, including cooperation in migrating the Site and URL to us or our designee; (b) return all Content and customer/user/order data in a commonly used machine-readable format within 30 days of the Termination Date; and (c) delete and certify deletion thereafter — with express self-survival to work around the narrow Section 10.7 list.

This is the preferred playbook position, reached with a single insertion and no changes to the negotiated Termination Payment mechanics. The comment offers the 90-day assistance fallback if HDI pushes back on the six-month tail.
